  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Biosecurity Partnerships Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT and DAFF entered into the Pacific Biosecurity Partnerships Program (PBPP) in 2020 to: drive agricultural sector growth; promote market access and biosecurity compliance for Pacific agricultural exports; and support regional food security outcomes by strengthening Pacific biosecurity, animal health and plant protection capability.&#xa0; In addition, PBPP enables Australia to implement its PACER Plus biosecurity commitments to facilitate greater trade with Pacific Island countries. PBPP complements other Australian investments in the region, for example by working closely with the Pacific Horticultural and Agricultural Market Access Program and the Market Development Facility Program.</narrative>
  </description>
